Continue the existing UX/UI system for the digital multimedia library “Мирас — Культура и традиционные знания Центральной Азии”.

IMPORTANT:
Do not redesign the existing homepage or catalog page.
Use the same established visual language and shared components.

EXISTING VISUAL SYSTEM:

* Background: warm off-white #FAF8F4
* Primary: deep ink blue #1C3A5E
* Accent: terracotta/ochre #B85A2A
* Heading font: Playfair Display
* Body/interface: Inter
* Metadata/labels: DM Mono
* Serious cultural institution / editorial digital library aesthetic
* No SaaS dashboard styling
* No excessive ethnic decoration
* No stereotypical Central Asian ornament
* Strong readability and generous whitespace
* Shared Header and Footer already exist
* Existing reusable material cards and TypeBadge already exist
* Desktop and mobile responsive behavior required

Build the remaining PUBLIC-FACING pages and states.

==================================================

1. SEARCH RESULTS PAGE
   ==================================================

Create a dedicated search results page for queries such as:

“Манас”

The search must work across:

* titles
* alternative names
* authors
* metadata
* descriptions
* keywords
* full text
* OCR text from scanned publications
* transcripts and subtitles from video/audio
* image captions

PAGE STRUCTURE:

Header

Breadcrumb:
Главная / Поиск

Large heading:
Результаты поиска

Large search input containing the active query.

Example:
“Манас”

Below search:
Show result count.

Example:
“Найдено 128 материалов”

FILTERS:
Reuse the visual logic of the Catalog filters:

* Material type
* Knowledge area
* Author
* Country, multi-select
* Language
* Year / period
* Region
* File availability

SEARCH RESULT CARDS:
Each card must display:

* material type
* title
* author/creator
* country
* year
* language
* image/thumbnail when relevant
* short text snippet

Most importantly:
show WHERE the match was found.

Examples:
“Найдено в названии”
“Найдено в OCR”
“Найдено в транскрипте”
“Найдено в описании”
“Найдено в имени автора”

Highlight the matching word in the snippet.

Example:

Найдено в OCR:
“…эпическое сказание Манас занимает особое место…”

Include sorting:

* Relevance
* Newest
* Title

Include pagination.

Also design:

* no results state
* loading state
* query suggestions / related terms

Do not turn this into a generic ecommerce search page.

==================================================
2. PUBLICATION / BOOK DETAIL PAGE
=================================

Create a detailed page for a publication such as a book, article, manuscript or report.

Example content:
Title: Манас
Material type: Книга

PAGE STRUCTURE:

Breadcrumb

Material type badge

Large Playfair Display title

Alternative/original title if available

Main two-column layout.

LEFT / MAIN CONTENT:

* Cover image or document preview
* Description / abstract
* Table of contents if available
* bibliographic information
* related themes
* knowledge areas
* linked countries and regions
* linked authors

RIGHT / INFORMATION PANEL:
Clearly structured metadata:

* Author
* Publication year
* Language
* Country
* Region
* Material type
* Knowledge area
* Source
* Citation
* Rights / license
* Access status

FILE SECTION:

If PDF is publicly viewable:
Show:
“Открыть документ”

If downloadable:
Show:
“Скачать PDF”

If view-only:
Explain:
“Доступно только для просмотра”

If restricted:
Show:
“Запросить доступ”

Design an embedded PDF/document preview area.

RELATED MATERIALS:
Show related:

* books
* articles
* videos
* audio
* photographs
* traditional knowledge

Also include:
“Об авторе”
“Связанные традиционные знания”

==================================================
3. VIDEO / AUDIO DETAIL PAGE
============================

Create a media detail page.

Support both VIDEO and AUDIO variants.

VIDEO:

* large video player
* poster image
* duration
* subtitles control

AUDIO:

* accessible audio player
* waveform or simple editorial audio UI
* duration

Metadata:

* title
* participants
* creators
* country
* region
* year
* language
* knowledge areas
* rights
* source

TRANSCRIPT SECTION:
This is important.

Show a transcript with timestamps.

Example:

00:01:24
“…Манас…”

00:03:18
“…традиция исполнения…”

Allow the user to:

* read transcript
* jump to timestamp
* search within transcript

If subtitles exist, indicate language.

RELATED MATERIALS:
Show linked publications, photos, authors, countries and traditional knowledge records.

==================================================
4. TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE DETAIL PAGE
====================================

This is one of the most important pages of the platform.

This is NOT a normal article page.

It represents a traditional knowledge / cultural practice entity.

Example:
“Эпос Манас”

PAGE STRUCTURE:

Breadcrumb

Knowledge category label

Large title

Alternative names / transliterations

Short introduction

MAIN CONTENT:

* detailed description
* history / context
* transmission / preservation
* associated regions
* communities / knowledge holders
* countries
* knowledge categories

Show structured relationships.

RELATED MATERIALS:
Create sections such as:

Публикации — 24
Видео — 11
Аудио — 8
Фотографии — 36

Each section uses the shared material cards.

PEOPLE / COMMUNITIES:
Show linked:

* performers
* researchers
* authors
* communities
* knowledge holders

GEOGRAPHY:
Show associated:

* countries
* regions
* places

RIGHTS / ETHICS:
Include a visible but non-intrusive information block for:

* source
* rights
* consent
* restrictions
* attribution

The page should feel like the central hub connecting all related knowledge.

==================================================
5. AUTHOR / PERSON PAGE
=======================

Create an author/person profile.

Example:
“Саякбай Каралаев”

PAGE STRUCTURE:

Breadcrumb

Portrait

Name

Alternative name spellings / transliterations

Role:
Example:
Манасчы

Basic metadata:

* country
* birth/death dates if available
* languages
* roles

Biography

RELATED MATERIALS:
Automatically show all linked:

* books
* articles
* video
* audio
* photos
* traditional knowledge

Include filtering by material type.

Include associated:

* countries
* regions
* knowledge areas

Avoid making the page look like a social profile.

It should look like an authority record in a serious cultural archive.

==================================================
6. COUNTRY PAGE
===============

Create a country landing page.

Example:
Кыргызстан

PAGE STRUCTURE:

Breadcrumb

Hero area with documentary cultural image

Country name

Native-language name

Short introduction

Compact statistics:

* materials
* authors
* collections
* knowledge areas

SECTIONS:

Traditional knowledge
Show category cards relevant to the country.

Featured materials
Reuse shared material cards.

Authors / people
Show linked people.

Collections
Show country-related collections.

Regions
Show region navigation.

Latest / highlighted materials

Provide a clear action:
“Смотреть все материалы Кыргызстана”

Do not make it look like a tourism website.

==================================================
7. COLLECTION DETAIL PAGE
=========================

Example:
“Эпос Манас”

COLLECTION PAGE STRUCTURE:

Breadcrumb

Large editorial hero image

Collection label

Title

Curatorial description

Metadata:

* country/countries
* curator/editor if applicable
* number of materials

Below:
Collection materials

Allow filtering:

* material type
* language
* year

Use editorial layout with strong typography.

The collection should feel curated, unlike general search results.

==================================================
8. ABOUT PAGE
=============

Create an institutional About page.

Sections:

* About the project
* Mission
* What the library contains
* Countries covered
* Who the library is for
* Preservation and access principles
* Rights and ethical use
* Contact / partners

The design should be editorial and restrained.

No marketing-style SaaS feature blocks.

==================================================
9. ACCESS STATES
================

Design reusable states for materials with different access permissions.

A. PUBLIC DOWNLOAD
Buttons:
Открыть
Скачать

B. PUBLIC VIEW ONLY
Message:
“Материал доступен только для просмотра”

C. REQUEST ACCESS
Message explaining restricted access
Button:
“Запросить доступ”

D. EMBARGO
Message:
“Материал станет доступен после [date]”

E. CLOSED ARCHIVE
Do not expose protected metadata or files unnecessarily.

Create calm institutional UI for these states.

==================================================
10. SYSTEM STATES
=================

Create reusable components for:

* Loading skeleton
* Empty state
* Search no-results
* Error page
* 404
* File processing state
* OCR processing state
* Transcript processing state

Examples:

“Файл обрабатывается”

“OCR ещё не завершён”

“Транскрипт готовится”

Keep them simple and consistent with the cultural-library design.

==================================================
11. MOBILE UX
=============

Show mobile adaptations for the major pages:

* Search
* Catalog
* Material detail
* Traditional knowledge
* Author
* Country

Requirements:

* sticky search where useful
* filters become bottom sheet / drawer
* metadata collapses appropriately
* cards become single-column
* player remains usable
* document viewer remains accessible
* no horizontal overflow
* touch targets accessible

==================================================
12. GLOBAL COMPONENT CONSISTENCY
================================

Reuse or create consistent components:

Header
Footer
Breadcrumbs
Search field
Filter drawer
MaterialCard
TypeBadge
MetadataRow
MetadataList
CountryCard
KnowledgeCategoryCard
CollectionCard
PersonCard
AccessStatus
RelatedMaterials
Transcript
MediaPlayer
DocumentViewer
Pagination
EmptyState
LoadingSkeleton

Do not duplicate components unnecessarily.

==================================================
IMPORTANT PRODUCT RULES
=======================

The platform is a DIGITAL MULTIMEDIA LIBRARY.

It connects:

* publications
* videos
* audio
* photos
* traditional knowledge
* authors
* communities
* countries
* regions
* collections

Relationships between entities are central to the UX.

Users must be able to move naturally between:
material → author → country → knowledge → related material.

Search is a central product capability.

Do not require users to select a content type before searching.

The design must remain calm and understandable even with large amounts of metadata.

Do not create:

* social media features
* likes
* comments
* follower systems
* ecommerce
* gamification
* generic SaaS dashboard UI

Create all remaining public-facing pages as one coherent design system, using the existing visual language of the Мирас homepage and catalog.
